    "text": "Over the past decade, adjustments have typically varied only by $1.5 million in sometimes in the city's favor. This funding increase is primarily driven by two key factors. First, FCPS's operating costs have risen by approximately $300 million. We represent 1.7% of the total FCPS student population, so we pay 1.7% of their operating costs. Second, the city's average daily membership has grown by 161 students over the past two years, contributing $3.2 million to the overall"
