    "text": "Good evening, council members. I'm Jennifer DeSato. I'm the executive director of the Oshar Life Law, where it is to George Mason University and chairman of the fall for the book festival of our board of directors. Fall for the book launched in 1998, as Northern Virginia's oldest literary festival has been supported by the city of Fairfax, its inception, and that's nearly 30 years. The annual fall event spanning several days attracts approximately 10,000 people, attendees"
